6,Chatting in Chatino,https://lifeandletters.la.utexas.edu/2015/10/chatting-in-chatino/,"The Chatinos of Tataltepec are connoisseurs of crawfish and distinguish many different species (nxkweèʔ, tkúʔ, tyunù, saʔya, and at least three kinds of tatyà) that local Spanish calls simply camarón — or shrimp. The community is quite close-knit.","Chatino, Tataltepec",Otomanguean
